1
00:04:20,869 --> 00:04:26,869
The rich have always fed off the poor. This time, it's for real.

2
00:08:41,739 --> 00:08:47,739
Society is a comedy, horror, mystery film directed by Brian Yuzna.

3
00:13:02,608 --> 00:13:08,608
Bill Whitney is worried that he is different to his sister and parents.

4
00:17:23,478 --> 00:17:29,478
They mix with other upper-class people while Bill is more down to earth.

5
00:21:44,347 --> 00:21:50,347
Even his girlfriend seems a bit odd.

6
00:26:05,217 --> 00:26:11,217
All is revealed when Bill returns home to find a party in full swing.

7
00:30:26,086 --> 00:30:32,086
Bill Whitney, played by Billy Warlock.

8
00:34:46,956 --> 00:34:52,956
Nan, played by Connie Danese.

9
00:39:07,826 --> 00:39:13,826
Dr. Cleveland, played by Ben Slack.

10
00:43:28,695 --> 00:43:34,695
Milo, played by Evan Richards.

11
00:47:49,565 --> 00:47:55,565
Jenny Whitney, played by Patrice Jennings.

12
00:52:10,434 --> 00:52:16,434
David Blanchard, played by Tim Bartell.

13
00:56:31,304 --> 00:56:37,304
Society is a 1989 American body horror film directed by Brian Yuzna in his
directorial debut from a screenplay by Woody Keith and Rick Fry.

14
01:00:52,173 --> 01:00:58,173
It stars Billy Warlock as a teenager in Beverly Hills who begins to suspect that his
wealthy parents are part of a gruesome cult made up of the social elite.

15
01:05:13,043 --> 01:05:19,043
Society was originally conceived as a more conventional slasher, featuring
a cult of social elitists who engage in human sacrifice.

16
01:09:33,913 --> 01:09:39,913
The screenplay was reshaped by Yuzna, who introduced body horror elements such as the reveal of the cult being a
shapeshifting species that can literally feed on the lower classes, a concept he based on nightmares he had experienced.

17
01:13:54,782 --> 01:14:00,782
The film was shot in California in 1988 with Screaming Mad
George as the special effects designer.

18
01:18:15,652 --> 01:18:21,652
The film screened at the 1989 Cannes Film Festival, but went
unreleased in the United States until 1992.

19
01:22:36,521 --> 01:22:42,521
It failed commercially, though it received critical
acclaim from international audiences.

20
01:26:57,391 --> 01:27:03,391
In the years since its release, the film has garnered a cult
following and is regarded as influential in body horror.

21
01:31:18,260 --> 01:31:24,260
The film explores themes of high school, orgy,
transformation, secret society, cult.

22
01:35:39,130 --> 01:35:45,130
The tone is lighthearted and dark and mind_bending.
